{
 "encounter_id": "00626",
 "speakers": {
  "person_1": "PATIENT",
  "person_2": "DOCTOR"
 },
 "turns": [
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Good morning. I've kept a log since our last appointment, if that's useful. It's on my phone. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Brilliant, I'll look at it in a minute. Headlines first. How are you doing? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Mixed. The washing is still there. I wash my hands around thirty times a day, down from about fifty in the autumn."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thirty is still a lot. Walk me through what a typical day looks like."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Every time I touch a door handle, a keyboard, anything from outside, I feel contaminated, and I can't settle until I've washed."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Is the anxious feeling worse when you try not to wash?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Much worse. I feel anxious when I can't wash, like something terrible is about to happen. It builds until I give in."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "And your hands, how are they?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Sore. They crack and bleed in the winter. I've been using more cream."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let's go through the tablets. What are you on right now?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fluoxetine, 40 mg once a day in the morning. Then a small white tablet that the clinic added in the summer, I couldn't tell you the name, only that it's round with a line through it."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Okay, I'll look it up on your record, but for now I'll note that you can't name it. And the third?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Melatonin, 2 mg at night, when my mind won't switch off."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Good. Any thoughts of harming yourself?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "No. None at all. It's the opposite, I'm frightened of germs, not of dying."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Thank you for being direct. What's your background, health-wise?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "OCD, diagnosed six years ago. And I've had eczema since I was little."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Do you work at the moment?"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Yes, I work as a librarian. Handling books is fine, it's the returns bin I dread."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Pulse 70, blood pressure 122 over 76, temperature 36.4, oxygen 99 percent. And weight 61 kilos, which matches last time.",
   "pause": 15.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I've lost nothing, then. Good. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Let me see your hands. Palms up. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "They're not pretty. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Dry, cracked skin across both knuckles, with a split here on the right.",
   "pause": 10.0
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "It stings in the shower. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I can't rule out the eczema flaring on top of the washing, which would explain some of the soreness."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Could the washing itself be making the eczema worse? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Very likely. It's a loop, the more you wash, the more the skin breaks. That's why I want to push the therapy harder. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'm willing. The exposure exercises are hard but I did four of them last week. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "That's excellent. Keep going with those, and use a thick emollient straight after each wash rather than waiting."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "I'll set a reminder. Anything else I should do? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "I'd like to check your blood, a routine blood test, to make sure nothing physical is adding to your anxiety."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Fine. And the next appointment? ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Come back in six weeks, and bring the log again."
  },
  {
   "s": "person_1",
   "t": "Six weeks. Thank you, doctor. ~"
  },
  {
   "s": "person_2",
   "t": "Well done for keeping the log. ~"
  }
 ],
